<title>DENMARK: POLL-ANALYSTS SEE B&amp;O PROFITS 22 PCT UP.</title>
<headline>POLL-ANALYSTS SEE B&amp;O PROFITS 22 PCT UP.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ten analysts polled by Reuters on Monday forecast that Danish home entertainments group Bang &amp; Olufsen (B&amp;O) would post full year 1996/97 pre-tax profits 22 percent up on the previous year.</p>
<p>The panel foresaw an average pre-tax profit of 333 million crowns, compared to 1995/96's 272 million crowns, with estimates in the 350-316 million crown range.</p>
<p>B&amp;O's own expectations, stated at its annual general meeting in June, are for a 325 million crown pre-tax profit.</p>
<p>The result is to be released on August 13.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
